{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-39400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $29{x}_{1}$, where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-39400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-2)}{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15-4-4}{9+16+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n29{x}_{1}=29\\cdot \\frac{7}{29}=7.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-39400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e58d7b888ca7fb2c77aae9a825665d041b2181c4bdabccb37984f46a0b657d0c"} {"question" "q-39400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-39400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-39400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-81104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $20{x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-81104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-1)}{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-1}{4+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n20{x}_{2}=20\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}=4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-81104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e58d7b888ca7fb2c77aae9a825665d041b2181c4bdabccb37984f46a0b657d0c"} {"question" "q-81104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-81104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "14"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-81104" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-81141" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{1}$, where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{35}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{35}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{35}}\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{10} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-81141" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =x\\cdot {q}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{10} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)=-1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-81141" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e58d7b888ca7fb2c77aae9a825665d041b2181c4bdabccb37984f46a0b657d0c"} {"question" "q-81141" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-81141" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-81141" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-102320" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-102320" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-102320" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e58d7b888ca7fb2c77aae9a825665d041b2181c4bdabccb37984f46a0b657d0c"} {"question" "q-102320" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-102320" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-102320" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-102339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $6{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-102339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-9)\\cdot 4+8\\cdot 2}{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-36+16}{16+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-20}{20} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n6{x}_{1}=6\\cdot (-1)=-6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-102339" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e58d7b888ca7fb2c77aae9a825665d041b2181c4bdabccb37984f46a0b657d0c"} {"question" "q-102339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-102339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-18"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"} {"question" "q-102339" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071962/state.json" "file_sha256" "223a38fe18f276b7ae48b0ab835649fb780c64928719b8ee72b6d95a6401703b"}] "usage" {"q-39400" []} "basis" 2596 "retractions" [[17592186157707 :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of $R^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $29x_{1}$, where $x_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}$.\n\n$B = {\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}}, x = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 